irs likely yes. Use Write.\n\nFirst lang-guard.sh. Bash with careful patterns. Let me draft:\n\n```bash\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# 用途：android/ 技术栈守卫——A14 只允许 Kotlin/Gradle KTS 生产代码，A17 源码不含线路字面量。\n# 前置环境：bash、grep、find；GitHub Actions ubuntu-latest。本机不装 JDK/SDK，不跑构建；待 CI。\n# 运行命令：bash tests/android/android-shell/lang-guard.sh [--self-test]\n# 覆盖 acceptance：A14、A17（Android 端）。\n# 说明：AndroidManifest/res 等非代码文件不参与语言判定（A14 约束的是生产代码语言）；gradlew 包装脚本除外。\nset -euo pipefail\n\nHERE=$(cd \"$(dirname \"${BASH_SOURCE[0]}\")\" && pwd)\nROOT=$(cd \"$HERE/../../..\" && pwd)\nANDROID_DIR=${ANDROID_DIR:-$ROOT/android}\n\n# 其他语言生产代码扩展名（A14）；.java 明确违规（Android 只允许 Kotlin）。\nOTHER_LANG_EXT=(java cs py js ts jsx tsx c cc cpp cxx h hpp go rs swift rb php scala dart m mm gradle)\n# A17 线路字面量：验收点名的名称 + 明显硬编码地址（IPv4/URL）。\nROUTE_PATTERN='Line 01|OSA[[:space:]]*·[[:space:]]*01|([0-9]{1,3}\\.){3}[0-9]{1,3}|https?://'\n\nfail=0\nreport() { echo \"违规：$*\"; fail=1; }\n\nscan() { # $1 = android 目录\n  local dir=$1\n  local f ext\n  while IFS= read -r -d '' f; do\n    ext=${f##*.}\n    ext=${ext,,}\n    for bad in \"${OTHER_LANG_EXT[@]}\"; do\n      if [ \"$ext\" = \"$bad\" ]; then report \"A14 非 Kotlin/Gradle KTS 文件：${f#\"$ROOT\"/}\"; fi\n    done\n  done < <(find \"$dir\" \\( -type d \\( -name build -o -name .gradle -o -name .idea \\) -prune \\) -o -type f -name '*.*' -print0)\n  # 线路字面量只查源码/构建脚本（A17），排除资源目录。\n  while IFS= read -r -d '' f; do\n    if grep -nE \"$ROUTE_PATTERN\" \"$f\" >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n      report \"A17 源码含线路字面量：${f#\"$ROOT\"/}\"\n      grep -nE \"$ROUTE_PATTERN\" \"$f\" | sed 's/^/    /'\n    fi\n  done < <(find \"$dir\" \\( -type d \\( -name build -o -name .gradle -o -name .idea -o -name res \\) -prune \\) -o -type f \\( -name '*.kt' -o -name '*.kts' \\) -print0)\n}\n```\n\nCareful: the first find uses `-name '*.*'` to skip gradlew (no extension), gradlew.bat has .bat not in list. Good. `.gitignore` ext = gitignore not flagged. Wrapper jar fine. `gradle-wrapper.properties` fine. `.gradle` folder pruned. `build.gradle` ext=gradle flagged (good—KTS required). But wait, acceptance A14 says only Kotlin/Gradle KTS, and a Groovy `build.gradle` would be a violation. Good.\n\nPotential issue: `ext=${ext,,}` bash 4+, fine on ubuntu.\n\nA17 regex with IPv4 might flag version codes? e.g. version name \"0.1.0\" 3 parts not match. Compose `Modifier.padding(1.2.3.4)` unlikely. Fine.\n\nSelf-test:\n```bash\nif [ \"${1:-}\" = \"--self-test\" ]; then\n  tmp=$(mktemp -d); trap 'rm -rf \"$tmp\"' EXIT\n  mkdir -p \"$tmp/android/app/src/main/kotlin/com/example\"\n  printf 'package com.example\\nclass Main\\n' > \"$tmp/android/app/src/main/kotlin/com/example/Main.kt\"\n  ROOT=$tmp ANDROID_DIR=$tmp/android scan \"$tmp/android\" ...\n```\nThe script currently runs scan at bottom. Restructure function `main` and call. Self-test should invoke script recursively rather than internal state? Simplest: self-test creates fixture and runs the script with ANDROID_DIR env pointing at fixture. But script calls itself; the recursion's self-test flag isn't set. Use:\n\n```bash\nif [ \"${1:-}\" = \"--self-test\" ]; then\n  tmp=$(mktemp -d); trap 'rm -rf \"$tmp\"' EXIT\n  mkdir -p \"$tmp/android/app/src/main/kotlin/com/example\"\n  printf 'package com.example\\nclass Main\\n' > .../Main.kt\n  ANDROID_DIR=\"$tmp/android\" bash \"$0\" >/dev/null || { echo \"自检失败：合法工程被误报\"; exit 1; }\n  printf 'class Legacy\\n' > \"$tmp/android/app/src/main/java/Legacy.java\"  # wait dir missing => mkdir\n  if ANDROID_DIR=\"$tmp/android\" bash \"$0\" >/dev/null; then echo \"自检失败：Java 未拦截\"; exit 1; fi\n  rm java; add literal file; if passes -> fail\n  echo \"自检通过\"\n  exit 0\nfi\n```\nBut recursive invocation of the script with env ROOT relative path used for display only; ANDROID_DIR override works. Note top `set -e`. For forbidden case expect nonzero.\n\nCareful with A17 self-test: put literal in a .kt file `Route \"OSA · 01\"`; expect nonzero. Use grep patterns; create with printf including 